nucqcd patch of cubature 1.0.4 (Steven G. Johnson, https://github.com/stevengj/cubature), applied by Integrator/CMakeLists.txt with patch -p1:
1. hcubature_minEval: hcubature with a minimum number of function evaluations (convergence is only accepted after more than minEval
   evaluations), the interface of the 2010 adapt_integrate that nucqcd bundled until 2026-11. hcubature itself is unchanged (minEval = 0).
2. -DNUCQCD_LEGACY_SPLIT (CMake option CUBATURE_LEGACY_SPLIT) selects the rule of the 2010 version to choose the dimension to split a region
   (the largest fourth difference, the first on ties), which reproduces the results of nucqcd before 2026-11 bit for bit; without it the rule is
   that of cubature 1.0.4 (near-ties are broken in favour of the longest side of the region), which changes the adaptive subdivision for
   integrands with steps. The default is the rule of 1.0.4.
Made with diff -ru of the pristine tarball files hcubature.c and cubature.h.

diff -ru a/cubature.h b/cubature.h
--- a/cubature.h
+++ b/cubature.h
